        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/sony-soft-controller-buttons-patent-drawing-2-crop.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Sony Interactive Entertainment has published an intriguing patent for a new type of controller whose buttons can alter their resistance and tactile feel - becoming harder or softer - to adapt to what's being shown on screen. Sony initially filed the patent application with the World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO), the United Nations' patents agency, in November 2024. It <a href=\"https://patentscope.wipo.int/search/en/detail.jsf?docId=WO2026110304&_cid=P12-MPXZ4A-31241-1\">was officially published in May</a> this year, as uncovered by <a href=\"https://www.cheathappens.com/sony_patents_playStation_controller_buttons.asp\">Cheat Happens</a>.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/sony-controller-soft-hard-buttons-patent\">Read more</a></p>",
